From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pmic_glink: run the altmode and UCSI work after resume

On the TB321FU, plugging a charger while the tablet is in s2idle resets
the SoC: the journal stops at "suspend entry", pstore stays empty and
panic=0 rules out a kernel panic.

The GLINK interrupt is registered with IRQF_NO_SUSPEND, so pmic_glink
messages arrive while devices are suspended. pmic_glink_altmode and
ucsi_glink queue their work on system_wq, which runs right away: the
altmode worker drives the Type-C switch, mux and retimer, and the UCSI
connector change (with 0841) moves the data lanes and the orientation,
reaching PHYs and controllers that are already suspended. With
/sys/power/pm_test, "freezer" (no device suspended) survives a charger
plug, "devices" and "platform" reset like a real suspend.

Queue both works on system_freezable_wq, so they wait until devices
and tasks are back. This is the fix Abel Vesa proposed for
pmic_glink_altmode (X Elite, PS8830 retimer over I2C), extended to the
UCSI notification as the reviewers pointed out.

Tested on the TB321FU: charger plugged in s2idle, with and without the
G9 dock, no reset, the tablet stays asleep and charges, the G9 works
after resume. Known gap: a UCSI change notified during suspend is not
replayed on resume (no port0 partner until the next event); calling
ucsi_resume() from the driver's resume hung the tablet on resume.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250110-soc-qcom-pmic-glink-fix-device-access-on-worker-while-suspended-v1-1-e32fd6bf322e@linaro.org/
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@
 	alt_port->mode = mode;
 	alt_port->hpd_state = hpd_state;
 	alt_port->hpd_irq = hpd_irq;
-	schedule_work(&alt_port->work);
+	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &alt_port->work);
 }
 
 #define SC8280XP_DPAM_MASK	0x3f
@@ -502,7 +502,7 @@
 		alt_port->tbt_data = *tbt;
 	}
 
-	schedule_work(&alt_port->work);
+	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &alt_port->work);
 }
 
 static void pmic_glink_altmode_callback(const void *data, size_t len, void *priv)
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
@@ -506,7 +506,7 @@
 		pmic_glink_ucsi_write_ack(ucsi, data, len);
 		break;
 	case UC_UCSI_USBC_NOTIFY_IND:
-		schedule_work(&ucsi->notify_work);
+		queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &ucsi->notify_work);
 		break;
 	}
 }
